{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And Moses gathered.</b> From the entrance of the Tent of Meeting." "<b>To the camp.</b> Each man entered his tent." "<b>ויאסף.</b> A term of entering into a house, as in ״וַאֲסַפְתּוֹ אֶל תּוֹךְ בֵּיתֶךָ״ (Deuteronomy 22:2), and the root for all of them — ״יִצְבֹּר וְלֹא יֵדַע מִי אֹסְפָם״ (Psalms 39:7). This teaches that He did not bring punishment upon them until the righteous entered, each man to his tent (Sifrei)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:29.514458159Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}